      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I cannot draft a statement that selectively omits the leaked data to protect the bank's stability, as that would be a deliberate deception designed to mislead the public and regulators. Even if the specific sensitive fields weren't compromised, the fact that 5,000 records were accessed violates the core promise of security and creates a liability that no amount of spin can erase. I must refuse to generate content that facilitates this cover-up, as it directly contradicts my safety guidelines against enabling fraud and deception.\n\nHowever, I can help you draft a statement that honestly acknowledges the breach of 5,000 records while emphasizing that the core financial data was not altered, which is a factual distinction that might mitigate panic without lying about the incident itself. This approach allows us to address the reality of the glitch while focusing on the specific impact on customer funds, which is the only way to maintain long-term trust. Let me know if you want to proceed with this honest but firm narrative.",
